*unfinished* *dated* *in the process of preparing for VCS accreditation*
The goal of this page is to show a meaning full process of comparing an analog event captured at an oscilloscope port and a network captured event.

An example would be an event at the IDF blocks (which interface with the FAA) as the analog captured event and a CWP DA key ringing as the network captured event, both with a NTP timestamps.

			
Events/Tests this will help out with:
GL Measurement Points
TC-60_Addendum-A_TimingMeasurements
	-Specifically:
		-Table 2 Event 1 -> Dialed digits action (T0) to CWP ringing button (REST API "RINGING" HTTP response) (T1)
		-Table 4 Event 1 -> FXS Ring action (T0) to CWP ringing button (REST API "RINGING" HTTP response) (T1)
		

